A name directly followed by { is a class instantiation, not a variable
read, even when the class is not in the published inventory
(diag.undeclared_variable near-miss, issue #304). Built-in function names
(Len, Today) are never undeclared either.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE OpenPanel;
	:DECLARE oPanel, nWidth, dOpened;
	oPanel := PanelLayout{"pnlMain", 0, 0, 320, 240};
	nWidth := Len("pnlMain") * 10;
	dOpened := Today();
	:RETURN oPanel;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE OpenPanel;
	:DECLARE oPanel, nWidth, dOpened;

	oPanel := PanelLayout{"pnlMain", 0, 0, 320, 240};
	nWidth := Len("pnlMain") * 10;
	dOpened := Today();

	:RETURN oPanel;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
